# Docker rebuild after changes

After code, SQL, or env changes that the running stack must pick up, rebuild and restart Docker before treating the work as done. Do this without waiting to be asked.

```
docker compose up -d --build
```

- App source is bind-mounted, but `.next` is a volume — rebuild/restart so Next actually serves the new code.
- `docker compose down` stops Supabase as well as the app. If Postgres/PostgREST schema changed, restart the stack (`docker compose down` then `docker compose up -d --build`).
- Do not `db:reset` unless the user asked.
- Confirm `kautilya-app-1` is healthy and http://localhost:3000/api/health returns 200.
